  "description": "BUSKIL crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C70 H91 Dy5 O21 S4,C1 H4 O1,3(C1 H2 Cl2),2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.529-5.023 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.02-169.59°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy5(μ4-OH)(μ3-OH)4(L1)(acac)6]·3CH2Cl2·CH3OH·2H2O (H4L1 = p-tert-butylthiacalix[4]arene; acac = acetylacetonate); empirical C74H105Cl6Dy5O24S4. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ4-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 μ4-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
